what is POD
-------------->
pod is a smallest building block in k8s cluster

Applications will be deployed as PODs in K8s

## to create PODS we will use docker images 
To create PODs we will use Manifest YML file
for single docker image we can create multiple pods also, in single pod cannot have same containers
if we run application with multiple pods then we will get high HA and LB
PODS count can be increased and decreased based on the demand


k8s manifest yaml
-----------------
apiVersion:
kind:
metadata:
spec:


pod.yaml
---
apiVersion: v1
kind: Pod
metadata:
  name: javapod
  labels:
    app: javapod
spec:
  containers:
    - name: demojava
      image: dockerpandian/httpd:latest
      ports:
        - contianerPort: 80
    
kubectl apply -f pod.yaml   // execute manifest yml

kubectl get pods   // check the pods

kubect logs <podname>  // to get the logs of pod

By default PODS can be accessible only with in the cluster. we cant access PODs outside the cluster directley

to access Pods outside the cluster we need to expose them using k8s services concept.

# https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/services-networking/service/
-k8s services
K8S service is used to expose the pods for outside access.

Cluster IP
NodePort
