K8S NameSpaces

Namespaces are used to group the resources logically

    databse-pods  -> databse-ns
    
    backend-pods  -> backend-ns
    
    frontend-pods -> frontend-ns
    
inside K8s cluster we can create multiple NameSpace

each namespace is isolated with another namespace

kubectl get ns  // display k8s namespaces

kubectl get pods -n kube-system // get pods of specific namespace

## in kubectl command if we dont specify any namespace then it consider "default" namesapce

in k8s we can create namespace in 2 ways
    * using "kubectl creaet ns" command
    * using manifest yaml file
    
kubectl create ns kaizenns

kubeclt delete ns kaizenns

when we delete a namespace all the resources belongs to that namespace also gets deleted

-----
ns.yaml

---
apiVersion: v1
kind: Namespace
metadata:
  name: kaizenns
  
kubectl apply -f   ns.yaml

kubectl get all -n kaizenns
